    "updated_at": "2017-07-05T15:30:24Z",
    "body": "I'd be happy to accept a PR for either making these more distinguishable, or tweaking that section with w-nodev so that it's less confusing. Ideally it'd come from someone with design sense.\r\n\r\nPersonally I think it's OK as-is:\r\n\r\n- The difference between examples and variables/definitions is pretty clear as examples are longer\r\n- Variables and definitions can be distinguished by context usually (but I am less sure on this particular point)\r\n- Notes to authors describing usage are basically the same thing as definitions/requirements/explanations in the dev edition.\r\n- It seems OK for all code, whether it's a definition or a usage, to use monospace.\r\n\r\nBut I'd be happy to with changes as well.",
