    "created_at": "2019-09-02T22:33:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-02T22:33:55Z",
    "body": "Examples would probably be best styled like they are in the full edition: put “Example” in front of them. The italics can be hard to read for multiple paragraphs, but the examples are usually mercifully short.\r\n\r\n“Note” styles are as of today indicated with a slight gray background, but for screens in sunlight and High-Contrast Mode, it might be best to also prefix them with “Note”.\r\n\r\nOpen issues and warnings may also want symbols or prefixes for High-Contrast Mode users, as well.\r\n\r\nWhat about bold and monospace for defining instances of code?\r\n\r\n> The defining instance of an element, attribute, or API is marked up like **`this`**.\r\n> Other code fragments are marked up like `this`.\r\n\r\n--------\r\n\r\nI’d be happy to make a PR for this if you think it makes sense.",
